## Failures

None open.

### Fixed: thumb invisible and on/off identical in forced colors - was MEDIUM
Location: `src/components/switch/Switch.scss:144`
Before: thumb and track both computed to Canvas `rgb(255,255,255)` in both states; only a black border remained.
After: `@media (forced-colors: active)` sets thumb CanvasText, checked track Highlight, checked thumb HighlightText. Probe with forced colors: default thumb `rgb(0,0,0)` on white track; checked thumb `rgb(255,255,255)` on `rgba(5,0,73,0.8)` track; same for disabled and disabled-checked. Behavior spec 20/20 and `npm run check` pass.

## Re-audit (2026-11-15, working tree with root fixes)
- Invalid focus ring: keyboard Tab on `with-error`, `:focus-visible` true, `aria-invalid=true`: light ring `rgb(231,0,11)` 3px solid, 4.77:1 on `rgb(255,255,255)`; dark (`&globals=theme:dark`) ring `rgb(255,106,91)` 3px solid, 7.04:1 on `rgb(10,10,10)`. Border matches the ring color. The old 20% tint is gone.
- FormData right after `form.reset()` (no await): checked-by-default switch back on, unchecked switch off; `FormData` reads `a,on` and the inner inputs read `[true,false]` immediately, so the mixin renders synchronously.
- Forced colors still holds: default and disabled thumb `rgb(0,0,0)` on white track; checked and disabled-checked thumb `rgb(255,255,255)` on `rgba(5,0,73,0.8)`; the invalid story keeps the same thumb and track.
- Behavior spec 21/21 (`--workers=2`, includes the new invalid focus ring test). `npm run check`: only D1 and D4 fail (Figma round pending, expected); every other check passes.

